• an increase in inventories of $4.9 million due to acquisitions, growth in existing markets, higher inventory costs and normal fluctuations in our inventory cycle;

• an increase in accounts payable and accrued expenses and other current liabilities of $34.6 million due to the timing of processing transactions in our accounts payable cycle; and

